  1098	## §10 Acceptance blockers and open items
  1099	
  1100	1. **Type-preserving canonical encoding in `dao.jing`** — declared,
  1101	   inherited, and gating every identity use (§4.2). Until
  1102	   `order-normalize` (`jing.cljc:45-64`) stops coercing lists to vectors,
  1103	   `[:literal (1 2)]` and `[:literal [1 2]]` share an address, and any
  1104	   cache, projection merge, DAG share, object resolution, or ledger row
  1105	   that treats equal addresses as equal values is sound only over the
  1106	   restricted domain the `:encoder-domain` rule admits. Process lifetime
  1107	   is irrelevant. This design does not close the item.
  1108	2. **The observer-lane batch shape and the program-input predicate**
  1109	   (§9.2) — integration items with no design answer in this document.
