   702	### 7.7 Dependency closure is Datalog over the tuples
   703	
   704	UCF §7.6.1 computes `:yin.k/requires` by a conservative fixed point over
   705	values, code, names, and modules. The **code part** of that fixed point is
   706	the queries below, run over the flat projection of every reachable tree
   707	and the segment-qualified rows (§6.2) of every reachable segment. The
   708	value, name-satisfaction, and module parts remain the walk §7.6.1
   709	specifies; these queries supply their inputs and do not replace them.
   710	
   711	Extraction over trees (`$ast` is the union of flat rows of the reachable
   712	trees):
   713	
   714	```clojure
   715	;; names, every one, not only free ones (UCF §7.6.1, Names)
   716	[:find ?name :in $ast :where [$ast _ :variable ?name]]
   717	
   718	;; store keys read or written by code
   719	[:find ?key :in $ast :where (or [$ast _ :vm/store-get ?key]
   720	                                [$ast _ :vm/store-put ?key _])]
   721	
   722	;; FFI ops
   723	[:find ?op :in $ast :where [$ast _ :dao.stream.apply/call ?op _]]
   724	
   725	;; parked ids named by resume
   726	[:find ?pid :in $ast :where [$ast _ :vm/resume ?pid _]]
   727	
   728	;; effect kinds raised by syntax itself: the tag is the effect kind
   729	[:find ?tag :in $ast
   730	 :where [$ast _ ?tag & _]
   731	        [(contains? #{:stream/make :stream/put :stream/cursor :stream/next
   732	                      :stream/close :vm/park :vm/resume :vm/gensym
   733	                      :vm/store-get :vm/store-put :vm/current-continuation} ?tag)]]
   734	```
   735	
   736	Extraction over segments (`$code` is the union of segment-qualified rows):
   737	
   738	```clojure
   739	[:find ?name :in $code :where [$code _ _ :var ?name]]
   740	[:find ?key  :in $code :where (or [$code _ _ :store-get ?key]
