| 3 | Runtime bookkeeping inside the tuple | Fixed. New §2.6 gives a frame schema table: `:node` holds the immutable tuple; `:fn`, `:evaluated`, and position live beside it; `:operator-evaluated?` is dropped as redundant with the frame type. §9.1 now lists the cold and hot continuation arms with line ranges. |
| 4 | Dependency queries incomplete | Fixed. §7.7 publishes extraction queries for names, store keys, FFI ops, parked ids, and effect tags over both flat rows and segment-qualified rows; composition rules read callable effects from profiles, resolve parked ids against the carried slice, and define `:complete`/`:incomplete`/`:blocked`; it states the recast does not resolve cross-activation naming. |
| 5 | No shared structural validator | Fixed. §7.5 is a vector rule table (nonempty, mnemonic, arity, operand kinds, saturation, target bounds, terminator, argc); §7.2 requires both paths to call it before registration with matching defects, adds a malformed-input set including `[[:jump 9]]` and a multi-segment case, and explicitly supersedes UCF §7.3.4's projection-primary sentence. |
| 6 | Ledger rows illegal as datoms | Fixed. §8.1 separates the logical `[t op address ref]` notation from transactor input; address-to-address facts become local ledger event entities with addresses in `v`, citing `local-datom?` and `pad-datom`. |
| 7 | Reserved-id allocation | Fixed. §8.2 uses no reserved ids: the op is a keyword value on the event entity, validity stays in the reserved markers, provenance links use the metadata-entity mechanism; derive direction corrected to input=tree, output=segment; §10.3 rewritten. |
| 8 | As-of negation wrong | Fixed. §8.6 routes through `query/current` with its as-of argument and names the latest-event-per-`[e a v]` rule; §6.4 binds the name entity via `:yin/name`. |
| 9 | Content identity vs occurrence identity | Fixed. §2.5 defines occurrence keys `[root-address path]`; side tables and instruction provenance are keyed by them; §4.4 states the distinction; §8.4 keeps one event per attempt with input, output, macro, and call-occurrence as attributes. |
| 10 | Macro flag removal without replacement | Fixed. New §8.5 specifies `{:yin/code tree :yin/declarations #{[path :yin.macro/definition]}}` with binding, ordering, missing-fact, scope, and redefinition rules; flagged as the blocker in §10.5 without requiring the expander. |
| 11 | Hash chain not in objects | Fixed. §5.2 and §8.2 define content-addressed derivation records naming input, output, function, and contract stamp; verification recomputes under the record's contract and reports revision difference as `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`, not corruption. |
| 12 | Encoder blocker scoped to durable ledgers | Fixed. §4.2 gates every identity use regardless of lifetime and adds an `:encoder-domain` validator rule over a restricted value domain; §10.1 rewritten. |

