   667	
   668	Defects name a pc. Rules 1–4 of `yin.vm.semantic.md` §2.6 (one segment,
   669	dense pcs, sorted by pc, refs resolve to entities) are satisfied by the
   670	vector form by construction and have no rule here; rules 5 and 6 and the
   671	UCF §7.3.4 checks are translated as follows.
   672	
   673	| Rule | Defect when |
   674	|---|---|
   675	| `:nonempty` | the vector has no instructions |
   676	| `:mnemonic` | the first element is not a mnemonic of `code/mnemonics` (`code.cljc:12-16`) |
   677	| `:arity` | the tuple's count differs from the mnemonic's arity in `yin.vm.semantic.md` §2.4 as saturated by UCF §7.3.2 |
   678	| `:operand-kind` | an operand is not of its kind: `:const` and `:store-put` values fail `plain-data?`, a `:var` name is not a symbol, a `:closure` params is not a vector of symbols, a `:store-get`/`:store-put` key is neither symbol nor keyword, a `:ffi-call` op or `:resume` parked id is not a keyword, a `:gensym` prefix is not a string |
   679	| `:saturation` | a saturated operand (`:gensym` prefix, `:stream-make` buffer, `:call` tail?, `:ffi-call` argc) is nil |
   680	| `:target-bounds` | a `:jump`/`:branch-false` target or a `:closure` body is not an integer in `[0, length)` |
   681	| `:terminator` | the last instruction is not in `code/terminators` (`code.cljc:19-21`) |
   682	| `:argc` | a `:call`/`:ffi-call` argc is not a non-negative integer |
   683	| `:encoder-domain` | a `:const` or `:store-put` value contains a list (§4.2); removed with the encoding |
   684	
   685	The address check (the vector hashes to the address it claims) is UCF
   686	§7.3.4's and runs before these rules whenever an address is claimed; a
   687	correct hash is never structural validation. The failure outcome of both
   688	checkers on the UCF lowering path is `:yin.k/undecodable` naming the pc or
   689	path, as §7.3.4 already specifies; on a local load it is a load error
